    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0192" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-04-05T18:00:00+08:00">April 5, 1948—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:37 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>611. We have read with interest Strong’s report on visit Tsinan, your 129 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">119</hi>] April 2, repeated Department as 52. Unless
                    Department directs to contrary, we suggest utmost reserve in considering
                    requests from regional leaders such as that made by Hsu to Strong for regional
                    aid. Time has not yet come, we believe, when channel other than that of central
                    government could be considered.</p>
                <p>Sent Tsingtao as 65, repeated Department 611.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
